   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "הַמַּכֶּה מַכֶּה בְּיָדוֹ. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: אֵין מַעֲמִידִין חַזָּנִין אֶלָּא חֲסֵירֵי כֹחַ וִיתֵירֵי מַדָּע. רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: אֲפִילּוּ חֲסֵירֵי מַדָּע וִיתֵירֵי כֹּחַ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And the» attendant «flogging» the one receiving lashes «flogs» him «with» one «hand» with all his strength. «The Sages taught:» For the administration of lashes, the court «appoints only attendants» who are «lacking in strength and» are «exceedingly knowledgeable» in Torah. «Rabbi Yehuda says:» The court may appoint «even» those who are «lacking in knowledge and» are «exceedingly strong.»"
  }
 ],
